{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0583","billNumberShort":"H.B. 583","billNumberLong":"HB0583","fileNumber":"2026FL0239","shortTitle":"Initiative and Referenda Signature Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"STODDA","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Stoddard, Andrew","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill creates a process to cure an initiative or referendum petition signature that is declared invalid.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>establishes a process to cure a signature on an initiative or referendum petition that is declared invalid by a county clerk because the signature does not match the signature on file in the statewide voter registration database;<hr><ltbullet>requires a county clerk to notify an individual described above when the county clerk determines that the individual's signature does not match the signature on file;<hr><ltbullet>allows the individual to cure the invalid signature by delivering to the county clerk a signed affidavit attesting to the validity of the signature;<hr><ltbullet>establishes deadlines related to the processes described above; and<hr><ltbullet>provides that a county clerk may not count the individual's signature as valid unless the affidavit is timely received.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Michael Cipriano","fiscalAnalyst":"Kiki Hudson","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"YIPXSILBMK","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-18 09:36:35.253","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel